- op: discuss  # 8949
  at: '2026-09-09T09:02:23Z'  # 8949
  by: agent  # 8949
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8949
  clock: 5  # 8949
  nonce: '8949'  # 8949
  message: "BLOCKER RE-POINTED 2026-09-09, INV-linub -> WI-nanom. Owner-authorised. Title\nupdated to match; the edge now reads WI-nanom blocks WI-mifag.\n\nWHY INV-linub WAS THE WRONG BLOCKER. It is the class for a CATALOGUED I/O call\nsite reaching its CATALOGUE entry through the F3 gate. This item needs FIRST-PARTY\nmethod resolution in the call graph -- telling `Store.add` from `set.add` on\nhypergumbo's own self-map. Same capability family (receiver typing), different\nconsumer, and closing INV-linub would not have delivered it. Read in the code\nrather than inferred from the titles, 2026-09-09.\n\nWHAT THIS ITEM ACTUALLY NEEDS, and it is TWO capabilities rather than the one the\ndeliverable list implies:\n\n  1. CALL-GRAPH SIDE. Python method call edges must resolve to the owning type,\n     so a `calls` edge into `Store.add` is distinguishable from one into\n     `set.add`. Partly shipped (PR #254 constructor-root typing, #752, and the\n     WI-zamud setUp-fixture field binding in #851); coverage on the shapes THIS\n     tree uses is unmeasured.\n\n  2. DEMOTION-ARM SIDE, WHICH THE FOUR-STEP DELIVERABLE UNDERSTATES.\n     `collect_production_references` is a standalone stdlib-`ast` walk over\n     production files with NO analyzer involvement, and at\n     `test_only_reachability.py:169` it indexes the bare attribute:\n\n         _index(refs.loads, node.attr, rel)\n\n     so `set.add` and `Store.add` both land in `refs.loads[\"add\"]`. This module\n     cannot reuse py.py's receiver typing as written. Step 2 of the deliverable\n     (\"make demotion_reason resolve a method reference through the receiver\n     type\") therefore is NOT a local edit to demotion_reason: either this module\n     grows its own type inference (duplicating py.py -- wrong), or production\n     references get sourced from the analyzer's IR instead of a second AST pass.\n\nWHY WI-nanom. It is the declared architecture for receiver typing (ADR-0012,\nspec section 20 multi-fidelity coexistence), already shipped for Rust via\nrust-analyzer's SCIP output, owner-directed 2026-08-23 (\"we should move forward\nwith INV-fibis/INV-nuhun under the assumption that we will add pyright etc in due\ncourse\"), and it is the only candidate that covers need 2 as well as need 1 -- a\nplain AST walk can never get types on its own, so an external type oracle is the\ncheap route. Carries its own gate: scip-python is an npm package, not PyPI, and\nAGENTS.md's allowlist names pip; that is a governance question before build.\n\nENABLING SIBLING, NOT THE BLOCKER: WI-kutal (python self.method() DST resolves\nthrough the flat bare-name last-write-wins symbol_by_name dict, py.py Case-2a).\nSame MECHANISM as this item's problem, different SITE -- it is the `self.method()`\ncallee endpoint, where this item mostly needs `obj.method()` on external\nreceivers. Its recommended fix (ADD a qualified `Class.method` key at py.py ~2453,\nsince a dotted key cannot clobber a bare identifier) would build the key space\nthis item needs, so it is worth landing first if WI-nanom stalls on the npm\nquestion. It is also the best-evidenced item in the family: reproduced at tip\n2026-09-07, 2 of 37 self.save()/self.delete() sites on pretix, and costed as a\nfalse positive in TWO measurements (0016 and 0021).\n\nSTALE PROSE LEFT BEHIND, recorded so it is not lost: the module docstring of\n`packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/test_only_reachability.py` still\nreads \"Deciding a method needs receiver typing, which is INV-linub's open work.\"\nThat sentence needs the same re-point and cannot be fixed from the tracker."  # 8949
